"Turner's cash edge and GOP attacks on Knickerbocker's work history"], "rationale": "Turner's incumbency, the district's Republican lean, a Likely R consensus among raters, and market pricing near 80 percent for him point to a Republican hold. A favorable midterm environment for Democrats and a mid-October party-sponsored poll showing Knickerbocker narrowly ahead keep the race competitive but leave her short of favored.", "watch": "Independent polling confirming or contradicting the Democratic-sponsored numbers, or the work-history attacks gaining traction, could move the rating either way.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Mike Turner (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Republican Mike Turner, the incumbent, seeks another term in a Dayton-area seat that leans Republican by about four points under the new map. Democratic challenger Kristina Knickerbocker has run a well-funded campaign, raising more than $880,000, and a Democratic-sponsored poll in mid-October showed her narrowly ahead. Most raters still call the race likely or leaning Republican, however, and markets give Turner roughly an 80 percent chance of winning.\n\nThe national midterm environment appears favorable to Democrats, which keeps the contest competitive on paper. But Turner's incumbency, his fundraising edge, and Republican attacks on Knickerbocker's work history give him the advantage. A Libertarian candidate is also on the ballot but is not a significant factor.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1787, "margin": -5.46}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.1387, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1203, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.155, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1216, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.119, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.1452, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.1169, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.1457, "margin": -7.0}, {"date":